From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:36:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: skip NAPI deletion on RX queues without a NAPI

While WED is active, WED RRO queues have no NAPI: DMA init skips
them, and mt7996 adds their NAPIs only without WED. DMA cleanup
deletes the NAPI of every RX queue. Deletion of a NAPI takes the
netdev lock through its device pointer, and that pointer is NULL for
a NAPI that the driver never added. A driver unbind or module removal
on a WED board with hardware RRO therefore dereferences a NULL
pointer.

DMA cleanup deletes only the NAPIs that a driver added.

Fixes: d0217732f96e ("wifi: mt76: Do not always enable NAPIs for WED RRO queues")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 dma.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -1217,7 +1217,9 @@ void mt76_dma_cleanup(struct mt76_dev *d
 	mt76_for_each_q_rx(dev, i) {
 		struct mt76_queue *q = &dev->q_rx[i];
 
-		netif_napi_del(&dev->napi[i]);
+		/* the WED RRO queues have no NAPI while WED is active */
+		if (dev->napi[i].dev)
+			netif_napi_del(&dev->napi[i]);
 		mt76_dma_rx_cleanup(dev, q);
 
 		page_pool_destroy(q->page_pool);
